==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A measure to show a change or relationship between two numbers as a fraction of 100, over a certain time.
#: {{ux|en|the annual '''percentage rate''' on the mortgage loan is 4.5%, indicating the cost of borrowing money on an annual basis, including interest and fees.}}
<!--#: {{ux|en|'''Percentage rate''' is used to talk about how much interest you earn on money, how fast something grows, or how something changes, making it easier to understand by expressing it in terms of out of 100.}}-->
# {{lb|en|finance|mathematics}} A [[coefficient]], expressed as a fraction of 100, of the [[quotient]] of two numbers over a specified period of time, where the [[denominator]] has the same units as the [[numerator]] but is adjusted by a unit of time. This measure indicates the proportion of a part in relation to a whole and is commonly used to describe rates of interest, growth, or change in financial and economic contexts, expressed in [[percentage point]]s.

